  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>OnKey listens to your singing to show how in tune you are. Your recordings stay on your Mac.</string>
  <key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
  <string>OnKey listens to the music playing on your Mac to learn the singer's melody. It never saves the music or sends it. In listening mode a short fingerprint of it (not the audio) goes to Apple's Shazam to name the song.</string>
  <key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
  <string>OnKey asks Spotify, Music or your browser (for YouTube) what's playing and controls playback when you press play, skip or start over.</string>
  <key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleURLName</key>
      <string>OnKey take link</string>
